A||||4||WisconsinGT||Head bolt question
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||08-24-99||02:23 AM||||Well, I ran into another problem today. I went to the local AutoZone to get head bolts for my 88 2.8. After looking on their computer, they gave me a set of Fell-Pro head bolts. I bring them back to the mechanic, he says, "does one of the bolts have a stud?" I look and cannot find one. For that matter no one at any auto store knows what I am talking about. Anyway, would anyone here know where I can get this very elusive bolt? Do I need it? Thanks
Z||000001||theogre||08-24-99||09:54 AM||||head bolt with stud....... It's a bolt that looks like a threaded rod with a nut in the midle. The part that sticks up above the nut is used to hold something down.<p>The question is what does it hold down..... If the stud is used like the one on the 4cyl it's just a ground point for the main battery cable. In that case move the cables someplace else and forget the stud.<p>Someone who's done a V6 care to add to that? I haven't seen what the stud portion is used for to be sure on the 6.
Z||000002||TOM||08-25-99||11:01 PM||||On the rear head they hold this little square shield. I dont know about the front one. I will look next time I have mine open. Just wondering why you need new ones.
Z||000003||ezsurf||08-26-99||12:36 AM||||Wisconsin,<br>I just rebuilt my 2.8.  None of the head bolts had a stud.  There may be one on the intake manifold, but not a head bolt.  I'd ask the mechanic to clairify it.  He may have been talking about a rocker stud.
Z||000004||FieroGT||08-26-99||09:35 AM||||I may be able to shed some light on this. <p>When I did the heads on my 86GT I noticed the same thing. One of the head bolts has a stud on the end with a nut. It's the one on the forward cylinder head closest to the battery. This is where the negative batttery cable goes. You have 3 choices:<p>1) Relocate battery cable. (I wouldn't)<br>2) Go to dealer and order that one bolt/stud.<br>3) Reuse your old one. (That's what I did.)<p>I had no problems after cleaning it up and reusing it. All the other bolts were new Fel-Pro ones. Good luck. <br>
